{# How the header bar and its breadcrumb look on every info page.  Each
   page renders `breadcrumb.jinja` into its page header, and the index
   page's tree module redraws that `#breadcrumb` from script (gain#1477,
   gain#2483).  One set of rules, so the trails cannot drift apart.

   Every crumb selector starts at `#breadcrumb` on purpose: the crumbs
   sit under `#page-header a`, which colours and sizes the About link,
   and an id-plus-class selector is what outranks it without touching
   that rule. #}
      #breadcrumb .breadcrumb-item {
        color: #252e34;
      }

      #breadcrumb a.breadcrumb-item {
        text-decoration: none;
      }

      #breadcrumb a.breadcrumb-item:hover {
        color: #4C93C9;
        text-decoration: underline;
        cursor: pointer;
      }

      #breadcrumb .breadcrumb-item.current {
        color: #24699E;
      }

      #breadcrumb .breadcrumb-sep {
        color: #85a2b9;
        margin: 0 2px;
      }

      /* The trail takes the size and weight of the header's links, so
         the current crumb -- a span, which `#page-header a` does not
         reach -- reads at the same size as the links beside it. */
      #page-header #breadcrumb {
        font-size: 18px;
        font-weight: 500;
      }

      /* About sits at the right edge of the bar on every page. */
      #nav-about {
        margin-left: auto;
      }
